# Upstream Yocto layer repos and pinned revisions for WendyOS.
#
# Sourced by:
#   - bootstrap.sh         (per-build clone into ${PROJECT_DIR}/repos/)
#
# The poky monolith has been retired here; "poky" is composed at clone time
# from three split-style upstream repos (bitbake, openembedded-core,
# meta-yocto). Each board resolves to a layer tree on disk via
# WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE; clones live under repos/${WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE}/<folder>.
#
# A per-board conf/template/boards/<board-id>/repos.overrides file may
# override any URL_*/SRCREV_* below (and WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE) before
# bootstrap.sh builds repos[].

# Layer-tree namespace under repos/. Boards on the same yocto series share
# clones; switching series (or running an isolated experimental tree) means
# pointing at a different tree. Every board is on blacksail, so that is the
# default; a per-board repos.overrides may unconditionally set something else
# (e.g. "wrynose", or "thor-experimental" for an isolated checkout).
WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE="${WENDYOS_LAYER_TREE:-blacksail}"

# Split-poky composition, plus the BSP and add-on layers.
URL_BITBAKE="https://git.openembedded.org/bitbake"
URL_OECORE="https://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core"
URL_METAYOCTO="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-yocto"
URL_OE="https://github.com/openembedded/meta-openembedded.git"
URL_TEGRA="https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra.git"
URL_TEGRA_COMM="https://github.com/OE4T/meta-tegra-community"
URL_VIRT="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-virtualization.git"
URL_RPI="https://github.com/agherzan/meta-raspberrypi.git"
URL_SECURITY="https://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-security"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The blacksail pin set.
#
# Every board builds on blacksail and shares one clone per layer under
# repos/blacksail/, so these values are the fleet-wide truth. A board file
# should override a pin only when the difference is genuinely board-specific.
# scripts/check-repo-pins.sh checks that boards on one tree never disagree about
# a layer they both use. Run it by hand after changing a pin — nothing in CI
# calls it yet.
#
# The whole set was re-resolved from upstream HEADs on 2026-08-04 (git
# ls-remote); the previous set dated from 2026-06-15. It had to move as one
# piece: oe-core gained an SPDX license-expression parser on 2026-07-15 and
# both OE4T layers converted their recipes from the old "&" syntax to SPDX
# "AND" a week later, so against the 2026-06-15 oe-core those recipes fail to
# parse ("LICENSE value ... has an invalid format"). meta-tegra could not move
# on its own, and moving oe-core alone would have left meta-openembedded and
# meta-virtualization seven weeks behind the core classes they build against.
# No upstream layer has cut a blacksail release branch yet, so master HEAD is
# still the only target available.

# Split-poky on blacksail. oe-core master declares LAYERSERIES_CORENAMES =
# "wrynose blacksail" and LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_core = "blacksail"; meta-yocto
# master and bitbake master (2.19.0, >= oe-core's BB_MIN_VERSION 2.18.0) match.
SRCREV_BITBAKE="c870f5bd96ad02efc02c58133c27bdae3a300e3e"
SRCREV_OECORE="2faf8e366df74aded7898904b72317521a08e2f6"
SRCREV_METAYOCTO="9c6cf36c3511b94957aba04002d98bec665e9f1e"

# meta-openembedded and meta-virtualization master HEAD. Neither declares
# blacksail yet — meta-oe says LAYERSERIES_COMPAT = "whinlatter wrynose",
# meta-virtualization says "wrynose" only. Both are bridged by
# conf/template/include/local/blacksail-compat.inc. Re-pin to a commit that
# declares blacksail once upstream bumps, then drop the bridge.
SRCREV_OE="0a60011ec174b91104a110c353cbf18748951270"
SRCREV_VIRT="526c97254fe43e0924df034aaa825f33ec30407c"

# meta-tegra master (JetPack 7.2 / L4T R39.2.0, Thor plus the Orin family).
# conf/layer.conf declares LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tegra = "blacksail". R39.2 is the
# first JP7 line to cover both Thor and Orin, which is what lets all five
# Jetson boards share one series.
#
# The work arrived on the wip-l4t-r39.2.0 branch, which OE4T rebased into
# master and deleted, so the old pin d0b2f4d81dc3 became unreachable. A commit
# no upstream ref can reach breaks the Thor CI build: bootstrap.sh's bulk
# `git fetch origin` cannot deliver it, a warm repo cache fails outright, and a
# cold clone survives only through the fetch-by-SHA fallback for as long as
# GitHub still serves the dangling object. Nearest master-side equivalent of
# the old pin is ceb73c72 — keep it as the fallback if master HEAD misbehaves
# on Thor; it is reachable from master, so it stays durable.
#
# There is no r39.2 release branch yet. OE4T cuts those as master-l4t-rXX.Y.x,
# so move to master-l4t-r39.2.x when it appears;
# scripts/ext/check-jp7.2-upstream.sh watches for it.
SRCREV_TEGRA="de0a5a233d4e5aff0ed64da39aeec9310ce693c9"

# meta-tegra-community master; conf/layer.conf declares
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tegra-community = "blacksail". Its LAYERDEPENDS pulls in
# openembedded-layer and meta-python, which is why those have to be made
# blacksail-compatible (see blacksail-compat.inc). Re-pinned from 931db8c0f56e
# for the same dangling-branch reason as meta-tegra. Fallback: 98d9e63.
SRCREV_TEGRA_COMM="f0beedf81977fe6cd28f39912c53139290f5a6f4"

# meta-raspberrypi master. Bumped from 3afc9728, which is ~10 months too old
# for blacksail oe-core — it trips renamed-variable errors like
# MACHINE_FEATURES_BACKFILL_CONSIDERED -> MACHINE_FEATURES_OPTED_OUT. master
# targets wrynose (one series back), which intersects oe-core's
# LAYERSERIES_CORENAMES ("wrynose blacksail"), so it satisfies the compat gate
# on its own. Pinned for reproducibility, since master moves.
SRCREV_RPI="a0ebcf5639b391690b27381cc65c56c157a0981b"

# meta-security, for meta-tpm (libtss2 + tpm2-tools/tss). Layered on x86 and
# every Tegra board — see bblayers/x86.inc and bblayers/tegra-base.inc — so it
# is cloned for all boards, like meta-tegra and meta-raspberrypi.
# Pinned on master: this is the exact tree the /data encryption stack was
# validated against on Thor, AGX Orin, Orin Nano and x86. meta-security has no
# blacksail branch yet, which is why the bblayers includes bridge
# LAYERSERIES_COMPAT_tpm-layer.
SRCREV_SECURITY="226839ac408223f8041cde1b1d8b762d6fbc8050"
